{"judgments": [
  {"clause_id": "c001", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The provision sets two different triggers — the Agreement is \"conditioned upon commencement of your employment\" by April 16, 2012 and \"void\" if employment does not begin, yet is \"effective upon the first date that all the parties have signed\" — leaving the operative date and the condition's effect uncertain.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.18},
    {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.09}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c002", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"You are expected to complete satisfactorily all assignments and training obligations\" is hortatory rather than promissory, and \"satisfactorily\" is measured only by Wells Fargo's \"sole discretion\"; whether this creates an enforceable duty is arguable.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.20},
    {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.07}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c003", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"At least initially, you will be eligible for overtime pay\" fixes no end point for overtime eligibility, and the phrase \"at least initially\" is open-ended on its face.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.31},
    {"issue": "The promise that compensation is paid \"in accordance with\" the New FA Compensation Plan sits against Paragraph 8's statement that the Agreement is only a \"synopsis\" of compensation arrangements and that plans may be changed unilaterally, so it is unclear which document governs pay.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.22}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c004", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The overtime cut-off is tied to the title change, but the trigger requires both licence attainment and \"graduation from the Training Program\", leaving the moment eligibility ends open where those events do not coincide.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.17},
    {"issue": "It ends overtime eligibility on a title change, while Paragraph 3 says overtime eligibility applies \"at least initially\" and Paragraph 10(b)(i) treats graduation and full registration as separate milestones; the milestones are not aligned across the instrument.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.16}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c005", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"May lead to consequences, up to and including termination from the Training Program\" states no determinate consequence, and \"your test dates will extended\" is missing a verb; both leave the effect of a failed exam indeterminate.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.22},
    {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.10}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c006", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The enumerated prohibitions (i)-(iv) on beneficiary designations, fiduciary appointments, powers of attorney and bequests are introduced by \"including without limitation\" language about internal policies, so whether the list is exhaustive of prohibited client benefits is arguable.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.15},
    {"issue": "The statement that this Agreement \"does not supersede or replace, in part or whole, any provisions of the Wells Fargo human resources policies and programs\" cannot be squared with Paragraph 20's declaration that the Agreement is \"the entire understanding\" between the parties.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.30}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c007", "issues": [
    {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.11},
    {"issue": "The at-will statement that \"You are not hired for any specified term or duration pursuant to a contract of employment\" is in tension with Paragraph 10(b)(i), which conditions forgiveness of Training Costs on five years' \"continuous employment\", and with Paragraph 8's description of the document as a mere \"synopsis\".", "type": 2, "prob": 0.34}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c008", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"This Agreement serves only as a synopsis of the compensation and other arrangements\" is ambiguous as to whether the document creates binding obligations or merely summarises terms found elsewhere.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.36},
    {"issue": "Calling the document only a \"synopsis\" of arrangements in effect elsewhere contradicts Paragraph 20, which states that \"This Agreement constitutes the entire understanding between you and Wells Fargo Advisors\".", "type": 2, "prob": 0.40}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c009", "issues": [
    {"issue": "The proviso excepting \"any Wells Fargo Advisors compensation or benefit plans or policies\" from the written-modification requirement swallows much of the rule, since the substance of the Agreement is compensation; the boundary of the carve-out is uncertain.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.26},
    {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.16}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c010", "issues": [
    {"issue": null, "type": 1, "prob": 0.10},
    {"issue": null, "type": 2, "prob": 0.09}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c011", "issues": [
    {"issue": "\"Wells Fargo Advisors shall be liable to you only for compensation earned and received by Wells Fargo Advisors\" is opaque about whose earning and receipt matters, and \"deficit balances (unrelated to the offset of the draw)\" is undefined.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.30},
    {"issue": "The unlimited recovery of \"fronted\" or advanced amounts on termination \"for any reason whatsoever\" sits uneasily with Paragraph 3's promise of a bi-weekly salary and overtime pay, which the setoff could absorb.", "type": 2, "prob": 0.18}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c012", "issues": [
    {"issue": "Employment is required both \"on the date such payments are received by Wells Fargo Advisors\" and \"on the applicable payout date\"; the two conditions are stated as one but are different dates.", "type": 1, "prob": 0.27},
    {"issue": "The forfeiture of \"any revenue or fees\" on termination is hard to reconcile with Paragraph 9(a), which preserves liability for \"salary earned but not yet paid to you prior to the effective date of the termination\".", "type": 2, "prob": 0.19}
  ]},
  {"clause_id": "c013", "issues": [
